#: ../../../extensions.md:1
msgid "Extensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../extensions.md:3
msgid ""
"It's easy to extend the xlwings add-in with own code like UDFs or RunPython "
"macros, so that they can be deployed without end users having to import or "
"write the functions themselves. Just add another VBA module to the xlwings "
"addin with the respective code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../extensions.md:7
msgid ""
"UDF extensions can be used from every workbook without having to set a "
"reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../extensions.md:9
msgid "In-Excel SQL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../extensions.md:11
msgid ""
"The xlwings addin comes with a built-in extension that adds in-Excel SQL "
"syntax (sqlite dialect):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../extensions.md:19
msgid ""
"If there are no aliases provided, tables are aliased automatically as `a`, "
"`b`, `c`, etc. as the screenshot shows. Since v0.33.5 you can, however, "
"provide your own alias/table name like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../extensions.md:31
msgid ""
"This is, you need to provide the table name/alias first before providing the "
"range reference as the next argument, similar to how the `=LET` formula "
"works in Excel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../extensions.md:33
msgid ""
"As this extension uses UDFs, it's only available on Windows right now. This "
"formula can be used on macOS and Excel on the web though via xlwings Server."
msgstr ""
